## Algorithm: compact intent, exact reservation, ordinary Git

1. Read the actual local Git HEAD and pin that exact commit as BASE before map
   construction/intake; never reuse a stale pins.head such as 83d3cc95 from an
   earlier observation. Before publication INTENT, owner uses existing evidence
   intake to save a canonical JSON
   path-to-SHA256 map in `docs/session_protocols/team-evidence-<sha256>.bin`.
   Reuse `_team_path_hashes`; no new envelope format. The map explicitly names
   ALL intended final source/record paths AND RESUME and GOAL_HISTORY. Stable/
   incoming source values are independently reviewed final hashes. The TWO named
   checkpoint values are SHA256 of their exact file bytes in the pinned BASE
   commit, read through Git objects, never hashes of current working-tree files
   or predicted future intake/checkpoint bytes. Their final bytes are bound in
   step 3. BASE must contain both verified checkpoint/history files. No omitted metadata, globs,
   nested maps, inferred dirty files or self-hash inside the map.

2. Save existing PUBLISH/INTENT, command publication, exact ID, subject
   `{kind:REPAIR,id:<same>,sha256:<map hash>}` and one operation.inputs map-file
   path/hash. The map file is thus explicitly declared, separate from its content.
   pins.head binds that actual BASE commit, rechecked after map intake has reached
   CONFIRMED and immediately before saving publication INTENT. Intake may advance
   checkpoint revisions but must not silently change BASE. A changed HEAD requires
   rereading/rebaselining before this intent, not substituting another BASE under
   an existing map. Optional existing operation.evidence
   strings `publication_incoming_commit:<40hex>` explicitly pin incoming tips;
   these are INTENT parameters, not completion evidence. Validate/preserve them.
   Recognize compact mode only for this exact publication subject and one matching
   content-addressed map input containing both checkpoint paths. Existing ordinary
   source-only inputs and non-publication effects retain their meaning.

3. Extend existing team-reserve-effect. Under owner lock, after existing remote
   observation, verify control, owner/installation/ACTIVE epoch, endpoint, pins,
   original ID, map bytes and Git ancestry. Validate map[RESUME] and map[HISTORY]
   against the exact Git blobs at the pinned BASE, not against the immediate
   previous_sha256 or working-tree preimages. Require current history to extend
   the exact BASE history bytes; validate its complete framing and contiguous
   checkpoint hash chain from the BASE checkpoint through the existing intake
   INTENT/CONFIRMED and current publication INTENT. Verify the exact current
   RESUME belongs to that history. Reuse existing bootstrap history-validation
   mechanics without its initial-migration/linear-Git restrictions. Ordinary
   intervening intake/checkpoint revisions are preserved and allowed; missing,
   corrupt, rewritten or unchained entries are rejected. Do not search for an
   arbitrary pre-intake prefix or require metadata to survive intake unchanged.
   Freeze full declared paths = map keys plus its separately declared input path.
   Capture post-INTENT RESUME/HISTORY hashes and reviewed final source hashes,
   modes, exact working/index/base preimages, map content/hash, owner/epoch,
   checkpoint hash, local/observed-remote bases and incoming commit pins in the
   existing private operation receipt, using _team_local_save.

   Incoming paths may differ from their intended final bytes, but must currently
   equal the base (or be absent at an absent base), with no unaccounted staged/
   dirty overlap. Existing owned dirty records are admissible only at their exact
   declared final bytes. Verify intended incoming sources against pinned Git/
   reviewed candidate evidence. Reject undeclared changes, traversal, symlinks,
   .git payload paths and deletions. Preserve modes; new records use 100644.
   No publication may silently invalidate current mathematical source pins; such
   overlap requires reconciliation/rebaseline before admission.

   An existing reservation returns RECONCILE_ORIGINAL, never a fresh grant or
   replacement map. Store hashes/Git identities and the map, not large file bodies.

4. Extend native team_guard with two narrowly scoped internal checks, no CLI:
   preparation checks saved preimages before native merge/commit; publication
   checks final working bytes AND the committed final tree. Caller passes its
   live writer epoch when a check persists the existing private receipt.
   Owner uses ordinary Git under that lock, merging the pinned incoming branch
   and preserving all parents/commits, then committing only exact owned records/
   checkpoint paths. No squash, source-copy substitute, add -A or foreign staging.

   Before push, guard verifies the declared full scope, final file hashes/modes,
   current source pins, final local commit/tree and base/incoming ancestry.
   Compare the final diff from the observed remote base: no unlisted changed
   paths; explicitly named unchanged paths are allowed. Preserve explicitly
   pinned incoming history; do not impose bootstrap's linear-history rules.
   Freeze the exact resulting commit/tree and durably consume its one native
   push attempt in the original private receipt. A competing/replayed guard
   cannot consume it again. This is a snapshot plus one attempt marker, not a
   second Git lifecycle engine.

   Necessary repair-admission edge: the existing confirmed-issue gate also holds
   publication at FIX_VERIFIED/FIX_COMMITTED, although FIX_PUSH_VERIFIED requires
   the publication itself (2178-2180 and 3048-3060). Add an exact verified-repair
   exception, not a global unhold: only the current issue's named repair subject,
   its positive independent FIX_VERIFIED candidate/source binding, its matching
   `<repair_subject_id>:publication` operation, actual owner and exact reviewed
   paths/bytes may pass. Other affected operations and unrelated publication
   remain held. Reuse existing repair-candidate/reviewer validators, checking
   canonical committed bytes as well as the reviewed isolated candidate; do not
   equate different commit IDs or invent a publication receipt. Publish the
   reviewed technical fix separately if required before a broader Mac/metadata
   publication. That does not split or copy the incoming mathematical history.
   The new confirmation records the exact actual remote commit required by the
   existing FIX_COMMITTED/FIX_PUSH_VERIFIED route. Those issue events follow
   observed local commit and remote proof, never falsely precede them to unlock
   publication. Extend lifecycle validation only if an actual mismatch with its
   existing exact candidate binding is demonstrated by this required test.

5. Release flock for the existing ordinary push of that EXACT recorded commit
   to origin/rh_clean. No force/lease/config/hook changes. The durable pending
   marker fences unrelated canonical writers during the network effect. The
   native recipe uses the fresh reservation and guard result; after a crash it
   inspects the original operation instead of executing merge/commit/push again.

6. Extend existing team-confirm-effect for TWO exact publication cases: compact
   publication and the tightly bound independently verified REPAIR source-only
   publication admitted in step 4. The latter must work without putting metadata
   into its independently reviewed repair-source manifest. For both, verify the
   actual local candidate commit/tree, exact verified source/snapshot hashes and
   fresh independently observed remote result. Keep its existing candidate/evidence contract; no
   arbitrary success string and no new user-facing receipt schema. Record exact
   local/remote commit/tree identities in its private observation. In particular,
   the remote_commit consumed by the existing FIX_PUSH_VERIFIED validator must
   identify the freshly observed published candidate, not the PRE-push base from
   team-observe-remote. Preserve that original base observation in the private
   publication evidence when recording the actual result; do not erase provenance
   or falsely reinterpret it as a post-push receipt. Observe network
   outside flock; recheck owner/epoch/snapshot before saving. Object-only fetch
   permissions are declared in the existing tool entry as needed.
   Exact confirmation is publication only, not mathematical acceptance or takeover.
   Other generic source-only publications and non-publication effects retain
   their existing confirmation behavior; this fix does not broaden that surface.

7. Extend existing pending guard and bounded plan recovery card for this native
   publication. Return the original operation/owner/snapshot/pinned commit when
   known. Original read-only reconciliation and confirmation are allowed through
   its fence; other writes/checkpoint replacements/launches stay held. A changed
   control cannot disable an existing pending marker. A lost map after reservation
   can be reconciled from the saved map/hash; missing/corrupt private state is a
   recovery blocker. Preserve partial merge/index state, never reset/delete it.
   Retry never repeats an unknown native action or creates another operation.
   Observe exact local/remote history; otherwise retain UNKNOWN. Do not invent
   NOT_EXECUTED or assume success after the remote advances.

8. After verified publication, existing resume-checkpoint may save confirmation.
   Publishing that later receipt recursively is not required: the published INTENT
   plus exact Git result is recovery evidence. A pulled home clone stays observer-
   only and reconciles original actions before new sends; existing release/claim/
   watch rules alone transfer execution. The repair changes none of those rules.

